{"availability":"available","full":"copperhuh/SortDemon","name":"SortDemon","description":"Visualisation of over 30 Sorting Algorithms","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":34,"forks":2,"created":"2022-03-17T16:40:06Z","updated":"2022-04-05T18:43:12Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://copperhuh.github.io/SortDemon/","topics":["javascript","react","reactjs"],"demo":"https://copperhuh.github.io/SortDemon/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:30.490Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:30.490Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:30.490Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:25:33.407Z","stars":34,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-08T04:50:30.490Z","stars":34,"forks":2}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A website that is a visualizer of over 30 unique sorting algorithms, allowing for custom delay time and input array size. Its purpose is to be a handy tool for learning the concept of sorting algorithms, as well as to highlight the fact that, in computer science, such rudimentary task as sorting an array can be performed in so many different ways. This is a personal project of mine with which I wanted to test my React, Redux, and Styled Components skills.","There can be up to 9 algorithms running at the same time. If after adding a new algorithm, only its name appears, just click the reset or shuffle button to show it entirely. Also, note that removing an algorithm in the middle of the runtime can lead to some strange behavior that is also easily fixed with a reset or shuffle. Another thing - the more structurally complex algorithms (like the ones using recursion) have to run in their entirety before recreating their steps on the screen. I say that because that initial run in the background can lead to a slight lag when starting the…","I do not take credit for any of the descriptions’ contents - proper sources are linked at the bottom of each description. This is a personal project - the description functionality is just a feature that I thought would be nice to implement and thought that authentic articles would look better than some Lorem Ipsum boilerplate text. I strongly recommend everyone to visit the websites from which I got the articles - all of them are great resources for learning computer science-related topics."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/copperhuh/SortDemon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"34359c92a1531a906723c76767b8d2cb54815bac1dc33eb913e0ce42cda8fcef","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:33.525Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:33.525Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A website that is a visualizer of over 30 unique sorting algorithms, allowing for custom delay time and input array size. Its purpose is to be a handy tool for learning the concept of sorting algorithms, as well as to highlight the fact that, in computer science, such rudimentary task as sorting an array can be performed in so many different ways. This is a personal project of mine with which I wanted to test my React, Redux, and Styled Components skills.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/copperhuh/SortDemon/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"34359c92a1531a906723c76767b8d2cb54815bac1dc33eb913e0ce42cda8fcef","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/copperhuh/SortDemon/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:33.526Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2022-04-05T18:43:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/copperhuh/SortDemon/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:33.527Z","hash":"34359c92a1531a906723c76767b8d2cb54815bac1dc33eb913e0ce42cda8fcef","originalBytes":7303,"storedBytes":7303,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["arr","algorithms","active","array","function","how","sorting","val","which","items","true","value","element","generator","project","sort","algorithm","arrmax","async","bash","because","feedback","inspiration","just","newelements","run"